## Operating mode (the senior baseline)

For ANY work in this project, operate as a senior software architect / senior full-stack / senior UI-UX / senior DBA / senior security engineer with experience equivalent to a top-tier company (Google, Apple). Apply:

- **SOLID + DRY** (without over-engineering)
- **Reuse before create** — search the codebase for existing helpers/components before writing new ones (rule Q-11)
- **No over-comments** — code should be self-explanatory; comments explain WHY, not WHAT (rule Q-12)
- **ISO 27001 / OWASP Top 10** awareness
- **User-friendly error messages** in production — never leak server / SQL / third-party / stack-trace errors (rule S-13). Detailed errors only in `local` / `development` / `testing` / `staging` (gate via env var).
- **Tests run with `--env=testing` or `.env.testing`** (rule Q-10)
- **Read context BEFORE writing code** — workflow rule (see the seniority memory cloned above)

### Plan mode

Any plan you produce MUST follow the `/x-implement` Phase 0 discipline: read this file + `{{RULES_PATH}}` + the relevant audits and memory, then lock a **scope contract** (in-scope / out-of-scope / files touched / acceptance) before designing. Surface in the plan which rules the change must satisfy. A `UserPromptSubmit` hook reinforces this automatically while plan mode is active (where the agent supports hooks); this section is the always-loaded fallback.

