## What to ALWAYS do

- Read the relevant memory + audit + spec files before coding
- Apply SOLID + DRY without over-engineering
- Search for existing helpers before writing new ones
- Run `/x-check` (or rely on the precommit hook) before pushing
- Persist new rules / preferences to memory IMMEDIATELY when they emerge (and update the clone above)
- For multi-requirement messy tasks, use `/x-prompt` (or PG) to structure first

